"alternative": "Sheikh 2021 (choose with pharmacist/local antibiogram): 'penicillins should be considered one of the first line antibiotics to treat infections in MG patients' (rare reports with ampicillin/amoxicillin); 'MG exacerbation has not been reported after the use of cephalosporins, sulfa drugs (including trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole), and clindamycin'; no clinical reports found with tetracyclines. If an aminoglycoside is needed, Sheikh 2021: tobramycin 'may be considered as choice of an aminoglycoside antibiotic'.",
"monitor": "راقب: تدلّي جفن أو ازدواج رؤية جديد، صعوبة بلع أو كلام، ضعف الرقبة أو ضيق التنفس؛ وقِس معدل التنفس وتشبّع الأكسجين. الخطر أعلى مع ضعف الكلى.",
